## Program Constraints

- One field has one editable authority. Current element envelopes and parent requirements are
  authoritative; indexed graph/status structures are rebuilt projections.
- Every mutating graph operation is guarded, revision-accounted, cycle-checked, and atomic with
  its required projection refresh or stale marker.
- Automatic proof uses only registered immutable checkers and predeclared recipes within the
  current authority envelope. Production, credentialed, mutating, cross-workspace, or externally
  costly checks still require explicit current authority.
- Clean state and release gates require zero unresolved governing orphans, cycles, conflicting
  lineage, unclassified commitments, or stale authoritative rollups.
- Provisional qualification corpus: 25,000 elements, 100,000 edges, maximum depth 128. Initial
  budgets are 20 ms summary, 50 ms first 100 blockers, 250 ms mutation through 128 ancestors,
  60 seconds full rebuild, and 250 ms hosted API excluding network. Evidence may recommend a
  revision, but cannot silently weaken the gate.
- Work2 is development-only. Work3 and Work5 remain explicit separate requests.

## Verification Strategy

- Compare incremental rollups with an independently implemented recursive evaluator after normal
  mutations, migration, fault recovery, rebuild, and randomized DAG operations.
- Exercise missing parents and requirements, unfulfilled parent requirements, shared children,
  cycles, conflicting assertions, tombstones, stale evidence, checker errors, lease collisions,
  superseded runs, interrupted migrations, old writers, rollback, and checkpoint rebuild.
- Verify CLI, reporter, and hosted dashboard present the same typed status without flattening it
  into lifecycle.
- Record exact candidate commit, schema/evaluator/recipe versions, fixture digest, target identity,
  timing distribution, changed-behavior observations, and recovery results.

